---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About Mindscaper — Mindscaper"
	description="Learn about Mindscaper, the association behind Soundscaper and Framescaper."
	canonicalPath="/about/"
	activePage="about"
	containerClass="container about-page"
>
	<header class="page-intro">
		<h1>About Mindscaper</h1>
	</header>
	<article class="about-content">
		<p>
			Mindscaper is a danish association founded by former Audacity team
			member <a href="https://leo.wattenberg.dk">Leo Wattenberg</a>.
			Initially growing out of an online tools collection for <a
				href="https://kw.media/en/tools">kw.media</a
			>, Soundscaper quickly became more and more capable until it finally
			reached a point where it had <a
				href="https://soundscaper.org/docs/start/how-soundscaper-compares/"
				>more features</a
			> than Audacity, the program we initially wanted to achieve parity with.
			Over time, it became clear that Soundscaper shouldn't stay a kw.media
			tool, but grow organisationally resilient: Companies and individuals can
			be bought out, while an association of creative people would remain in
			control of their own tools.
		</p>

		<p>
			If you'd like to join us in forging our own tools instead of being
			eternally tied to subscription services, ad-supported nonsense and
			trial versions, you can <a href="/join/">join us</a>. We're not
			really interested in your money (hence why this isn't a foundation),
			but instead <strong
				>we are interested in you: Your experience, your needs of what
				your tools should do, your goals as an artist.</strong
			> Software should enable people to be creative and help accomplish tasks,
			not create unnecessary friction.
		</p>

		<section aria-labelledby="association-status-heading">
			<h2 id="association-status-heading">
				Status of the mindscaper association
			</h2>
			<p>
				Mindscaper at present is an association that's still getting
				started. While we do have <a href="/bylaws/">bylaws</a>, we
				don't yet a have CVR number, bank accounts, tax-exemption
				status, and so on and so forth. As such, we don't collect any
				membership dues right now. In practice, what we have right now
				is a community (forum/chat) you can join, without any further
				strings attached – and of course the first two tools you can use
				already, Soundscaper and Framescaper.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
